<%--
Raw_Text_Display - renders a Raw_Text value on a live page.

$value - a Raw_Text instance (NOT a string)

The PRINTER component Raw_Text declares. Interpolating the value mounts it:

    <%= this.data.client.notes %>

Escaped, with newlines becoming line breaks. That second half is why this is a
component at all rather than a plain string returned from Raw_Text.print(): a printer
returning a string is escaped by `<%= %>` exactly as a string literal is, so it could
never produce a <br> of its own. The decision that this encoding's newlines are
meaningful belongs to the type, not to whichever template happens to print it - which
is precisely what used to be restated, by hand, at every call site.
--%>
<Define:Raw_Text_Display tag="div">
    <%br= this.args.value.to_storage() %>
</Define:Raw_Text_Display>
